Firmware and factory data
-------------------------

Qualcomm, Xiaomi and Cirrus firmware remain subject to their respective
licenses. Inclusion in a download bundle does not place firmware under MIT.
Redistribution permissions and notices must be established for each distributed
firmware set before publication.

Device-specific calibration, WLAN and Bluetooth addresses and factory sensor
registry data are read from the user's tablet. They are not public source or
shared firmware assets and must not be distributed.

Fingerprint integration
-----------------------

Optional device/fingerprint/oem source retains file-level BSD-2-Clause,
LGPL-2.1-or-later, GPL-2.0-or-later and Apache-2.0 notices. QSEE supplicant/QCBOR
retain upstream BSD licenses. Exact dependencies are in SOURCE_LOCK.json.
The fprintd original source remains external and hash-pinned; distribution of
binaries must include corresponding source/adaptation as required by its license.
OEM TA firmware, credentials, HATs, templates, raw images and private calibration
are not included in this source repository.
